          <change when="2018-03-16T04:52:19-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/Myrto%20Malouta">Vote - AcceptText - Yes! Palaeographically the ligatured syllable δι is better than σι and it is also supported by one attestation.</change>
          <change when="2018-03-03T12:19:34-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/mgelmaghrabi">Submit - I read Ζεύδιoς instead of Ζεύσιος in ll. 3,9 and 26, cf. the delta-iota ligature for the name Ροδινη as in e.g. l.6.The name Ζεύδις is very rare, attested in this form only in SB V 7559  also from Tebtynis, 118 CE, Ζεύσις is not attested elsewhere. </change>
          <change when="2018-03-03T12:15:37-05:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/mgelmaghrabi">Commit - I read Ζεύδις instead of Ζεύσις in ll. 3,9 and 26, cf. the delta-iota ligature for the name Ροδινη in e.g. l.6.The name Ζεύδις is very rare, attested in this form only in SB V 7559  also from Tebtynis, 118 CE, Ζεύσις is not attested elsewhere. </change>
